# OksaSDR tour, "On the air": each mode heard as it is, iPad landscape 1366x1024 (QT_SCALE_FACTOR 1.40625).
# 2026-11-12 evening. The video keeps this take's RADE part (3.763, cut after the speech); its SSB,
# CW and BC parts were taken again: ssb.plan and bc.plan with the 2.9 kHz phone filter (the user),
# cw.plan on stronger stations. Needs an audio output (the app's own DSP runs only with one; a
# PipeWire null sink here). Receive only; the radio's NR is put back off, the slice on 14.074 DIGU.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # On the air
caption Each mode as it sounds on the band right now, live from the radio.
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption SSB on 80 m in the evening: tap the frequency and type it. The band plan makes it LSB.
caption !mark 240,145
frequency-dialog
wait 1500
keys 3.680
wait 1500
keys <Enter>
wait 1500
span 10
wait 4000
caption The radio's NR, from the DSP flags, takes the noise down between the words.
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 2000
taptext NR ~543,401
wait 2500
close
wait 1000
caption 80 m SSB at 3.680 MHz, the radio's NR on.
wait 20000
caption CW: the CW section, and Autotune puts the signal on the pitch for the decoder.
taptext CW ~1263,82
taptext View ~1324,82
freq 3.5393
span 6
wait 1000
caption !mark 560,115
mode CW
wait 2500
tapname cwAutotune
wait 3000
caption CW on 80 m at 3.539 MHz, as it sounds; the decoder copies it.
wait 20000
caption # The app's own
caption Beat cancel (BC), the app's own, not in SmartSDR. In a phone QSO someone tunes up on your frequency: a steady whistle over the voice, worst in headphones. A broadcast carrier 1 kHz off the dial stands in for him here.
taptext View ~1324,82
taptext CW ~1263,82
freq 7.334
span 10
wait 1000
caption !mark 560,115
mode USB
wait 6000
caption Tap the DSP flags, then BC: it finds the steady carrier and notches it out within 0.15 s; the voice stays.
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 2000
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 9000
caption BC off: the whistle is back. Up to four carriers at a time, in the voice modes.
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 5000
close
wait 1000
caption -
caption # On the air
caption FreeDV: RADE digital voice, decoded in the app.
taptext FreeDV ~1263,141
taptext View ~1324,82
freq 3.763
mode DIGU
span 10
wait 2500
tapname radeButton
wait 3000
caption 80 m, 3.763 MHz: RADE stations in a QSO, as FreeDV Reporter shows them; their voice comes through the app.
wait 45000
tapname radeButton
wait 3000
taptext View ~1324,82
taptext FreeDV ~1263,141
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 1500
taptext NR ~543,401
wait 1500
close
wait 1500
shot end
slices
